// The feature set of venus-hee on the QEMU virt board.  It is delivered as a
// BOOTDATA_DEVICETREE item in bootdata-combo-qemu-virt only, served by the
// sysinfo driver and read back by //garnet/lib/features.  A feature is
// enabled by the presence of its node and disabled by its absence or by
// `status = "disabled"`.  Images for real boards (the mt8668 bootdata-fs)
// carry no such item and keep their all-disabled default.
//
// `fx run-venus -z` boots the SOS Linux with
// `earlycon=pl011,0xffff32000 console=vmlog-sink0`, and its root file system
// starts the shell on hvc0:
//   - vmlog: the VMM's PL011 at 0xffff32000 and the vmlog-sink back end,
//     which write the SOS console to the HEE debuglog ([VM:n]).
//   - pci_bus/virtio-console: hvc0, reached with `vmm shell` on the HEE.
//   - wdt-sink: what venus-hee on QEMU does without a devicetree (its
//     managed software watchdog); a devicetree without it would turn that off.

/dts-v1/;

/ {
  features {
    vmlog { };
    wdt-sink { };
    pci_bus {
      virtio-console { };
    };
  };
};
